A||||7||gtsonly||Car cutting out, why? Please help if you can!!!!||||11||
Z||000000||gtsonly||06-11-2001||12:30 PM||||I was driving my car yesterday and in 5th gear, about 65, the car dies. I put the car into 3rd, pop the clutch and I have power back. Wierd!!!  Again I was driving the car yesterday and the same thing happens but this time when I tried to go to a lower gear and pop the clutch, nothing, the car was dead. I rolled to a stop, tried to start the car and it just turned over, no iginition. I went back to the engine and pulled the wires to the coil, put it back on and pushed the spark plug wires down on the distributer cap. The car fired right up. Do I have an ignition going out? Any checks? Anyone else ever have this happen? Please help.<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||11
Z||000001||gtsonly||06-11-2001||12:48 PM||||I just did a search and found that it might be the ignition module. Are there any checks for that?<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||10
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||06-11-2001||01:53 PM||||It sounds like the ignition module to me.<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||cscougar||06-11-2001||02:11 PM||||My 85 GT was dying intermittently while driving down the road.  As if I cut the key off.  I replaced the ignition module with a GM Delco one and that was the problem.  Took the old on the Hi/Lo Autoparts and had it checked.  It failed on all tests.  Its a wonder it ran at all.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||gtsonly||06-11-2001||02:37 PM||||What was the price of the module if I may ask?<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||1
Z||000005||cscougar||06-11-2001||04:50 PM||||I had an AC Delco module from a used distributor and put that in.  Hi/Lo wanted $54.00 for a Borg Warner module but  I have heard that AC Delco is the  only way to go on ignition modules.  I plan on picking up an AC Delco one for a spare though.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||06-11-2001||06:50 PM||||I changed mine out just a few months ago, I think it was like $44 at napa or one of the local parts houses. not too pricy, and you olny need a screw driver to replace it if I remember right. just pop off the dist cap, and look for the little black thing like the one you just got (kinda 1/2 circleish if I remember right, w/ 2 plugs?) think it has 2 screws and a plastic clip holding everything in place. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fyerstarter||06-11-2001||10:15 PM||||In the past six months I have gone through 5 ignition modules between my two Fieros (87 gt and 86 gt). Two stock Gm ones, Two cheapy Autozone Wells ones, and one Accell Hi Performance Module!!! These things like to go out at the worst times so carry a spare. Also I used to recommend taking modules to autozone to get tested. Not anymore, I took the Accell one there to get tested as part of my troubleshooting and it tested good. So here I was for two more weeks dicking around with ****  thinking I have a good module and finally I put the module in the other car and all of a sudden started having the same problems. So I tossed it in the nearest garbage and got a new one and everything has been peachy since. ||||reg||1
